  "fieldNotes": {
    "truckGate": "Single signalized main truck entrance off 142nd Ave E (entrance pano IN9diRJmskbGzHSl2a5FxQ, 2025-03); the access-control checkpoint is an internal canopied gatehouse straddling the truck lanes between the north drop yard and the cross-dock, with orange lane delineators and queued trucks (z18/z20 sat).",
    "guardShack": "Internal canopied check-in/security building straddling the truck lanes (~47.2210,-122.2443) with cars and a tractor-trailer parked at it; larger than a 1-3-space booth so flagged uncertain, but functions as the staffed driver check-in point.",
    "postGateStaging": "Striped staging stalls and angled trailer-staging rows in the central yard just inside the internal gatehouse and before the dock faces.",
    "shipRcvSeparate": "Two distinct cross-dock buildings plus dock banks on multiple faces (north building south face, main building west and east faces) give physically separate ship/receive clusters.",
    "multipleFacilities": "Campus: a north E-W cross-dock building, the main L/T cross-dock at the roster coords, and a third smaller building at the south end.",
    "scale": "No distinct weigh-scale pad positively identified in the truck path; left false.",
    "dropArea": "Hundreds of drop trailers in dense rows on the west edge, east edge, and north yard; well into the 50+ band.",
    "railServed": "Mainline rail runs N-S in the buffer west of the property but no spur enters the yard; truck-only.",
    "urbanRural": "Sumner WA edge-of-town industrial park (Sumner Tacoma 142nd Ave E corridor); broader setting is small-town industrial, classified Rural per rubric tie-break.",
    "fastLaneOpportunity": "Wide entrance apron and multi-lane internal gatehouse give room for an express/bypass lane.",
    "entryLanes": "Estimated 2 inbound at the internal gatehouse canopy; exact lane count not fully resolvable from overhead."
